y_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Medibank Private Sale Bill 2006 - Second Reading - Funds to be used for public health care","noes":45,"question":"This division relates to the Policy _[For privatising government assets](/policies/21)_. The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-12-04.74.1) introduced by Greens Senator [Kerry Nettle](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Kerry_Nettle&mpc=Senate&house=senate). This means that it was rejected. The motion would have amended the [original motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-12-04.75.1) \"_That this bill be now read a second time_\" with the following: \"_At the end of the motion, add: “but the Senate is of the view that any funds raised by the sale of Medibank Private should be directed to public health care.”_\" Because this motion was unsuccessful, the original motion can now be put.(See that division [here](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/division.php?date=2006-12-04&number=6&dmp=21&house=senate). ) _Background to the bill_ The bill was introduced to allow the federal government to sell its interest in [Medibank Private](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medibank_Private) Limited and allow Medibank to operate on a “for profit” basis. The Coalition Government plans to do this after the 2007 election, should it be re-elected.(Read more about this privatisation proposal on Wikipedia [here](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medibank_Private#Privatisation_proposals) and on the ABC's World Today program [here](http://www.abc.net.au/worldtoday/content/2006/s1739241.htm).)","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1213","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2006-12-04/5"}
